          .proof
            %h6#proof_17 Proof
            %p
              It is clear from the definition that each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi 𝒮
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ρ
                          %mi vac
                      %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}^{\rho}_{\rho_{vac}}
              satisfies the axiom “perturbation” (in def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LagrangianFieldTheoryPerturbativeScattering"}
            %p
              In order to verify the axiom “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+additivity"}> causal additivity
              ”, observe, for convenience, that by prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CausalFactorizationAlreadyImpliesSMatrix"}
              it is sufficient to check
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+factorization"} causal factorization
            %p
              So consider
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi O
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi O
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi LocObs
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mtext BV-BRST
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ℏ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi g
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O_1, O_2 \in LocObs(E_{\text{BV-BRST}})[ [ \hbar, g, j] ]\langle g,j\rangle
              two local observables whose spacetime support is in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+order"} causal order
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi supp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi O
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∨
                      %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                      %mo ∧
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi supp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi O
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    supp(O_1)
                    \\;{\vee\!\!\!\wedge}\;
                    supp(O_2)
                    \\,.
            %p We need to show that the
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
